Boulder Highway built in 1931 to connect  Las Vegas to Henderson and Boulder City  now a very busy road and in need of a  major update Mary Jane beliesa explains  the improvements planned along Boulder  Highway  the project reimagined Boulder Highway  has been in the works for a few years  and is wrapping up the design stage the  project starts here in Henderson at  wagon wheel drive and continues seven  and a half miles past Gibson Road Scott  Martin a former police captain with the  Nevada Department of Public Safety now a  private investigator is excited to see  the changes as he used to patrol that  area as a former police officer I've  investigated  thousands of traffic accidents and I  have family that live on right off of  Boulder Highway pre-construction starts  in November converting Boulder Highway  to two travel Lanes in both directions  with additional Transit only Lanes in  the median and we're looking at  increasing the safety making it easier  for pedestrians for bicyclists for the  30 000 residents that live within a half  mile Boulder Highway project manager  Scott Jarvis of the reimagined Boulder  Highway project says this update is long  overdue as too many fatalities take  place along Boulder Highway each year he  hopes Redevelopment of this Corridor  will open up opportunities for  businesses and people to enjoy and move  in we are adding in added crosswalks at  a location for people to get from side  to side we're looking at modifications  to the side streets so there's not such  a long Crossing distance for pedestrians  I think it's important for everybody to  remember that it's a shared  responsibility amongst us all  pedestrians bicyclists drivers to ensure  that you're paying 100 percent full  attention to your driving the  construction phase is expected to start  on or before January 2024 and is  expected to end September 2025. Mary  June bellezza 8 News Now
 

